# Paths the self-contained gate (task/term/self-contained.ts) lets through: a test's fake root, a platform's own
# folder named in a comment, the product's own home. One per line: the pattern, a tab, then the reason. A pattern
# covers a path that is the pattern or goes on past it at a slash or a backslash. A path into the owner's own home
# layout is never allowed, whatever this file says.
/home/p	fake Linux home in test fixtures (cask scope, Documents and notes paths)
/home/me	fake Linux home in test fixtures (language server roots, package store paths)
/Users/me	fake macOS home in test fixtures (format-path)
/Users/a	fake macOS home in test fixtures (self-manager, a source checkout)
C:\Users\p	fake Windows profile in test fixtures (cask scope)
C:\Users\a	fake Windows profile in test fixtures (self-manager, winget paths)
D:/Users/p	fake Windows profile on a second drive in test fixtures (cask scope)
C:/Users/Domenic	WPT URL test data (test/stdlib/url/urltestdata.json), a file URL from jsdom's own tests
/etc/hosts	a system file used as a path outside any project in format-path tests
/var/folders	the macOS temporary folder, named in comments about its two spellings
/private/var	the macOS temporary folder's real path, named in comments about its two spellings
~/.base/	the product's own home, where Term keeps installs, caches and the auth token
/home/user	fake Linux home in a stdlib path test (edge-path.tree)
~/.term	the product's home before it moved under ~/.base, in output mockups and older tool comments
~/.seed	the product's home under its old name, Seed, in a publishing tool
~/.ssh	the ssh folder, where a remote test machine's key and known hosts are
~/.m2	the maven repository, named in the kotlin toolchain script
~/shape	fake project folder in the terminal output fixtures and mockups
~/other	fake path outside the project in format-path tests
~/x	fake project folder in a knit output test
~/Library	the macOS folder for an application's own files, named in comments
~/.local/share	the XDG data folder on Linux, named in comments and the dev bootstrap
~/.docker	the docker config folder, the registry credentials' last fallback
~/.zshrc	a shell profile, in install instructions the CLI prints
~/.zprofile	a shell profile, in install instructions the CLI prints
~/.bashrc	a shell profile, in install instructions the CLI prints
~/.bash_profile	a shell profile, in install instructions the CLI prints
~/Documents	an example scope pattern in a comment
~/work	an example folder in a comment about project names
~/book	an example glob in a comment about the glob reader
~/...	a placeholder for any path under the home folder, in a comment
~/{rest}	the template that writes a path under the home folder (load-words.tree)
